{"base_rate":0.20818505338078291,"brier":0.0817688612099644,"bss":0.5039622740804763,"bss_hi":0.5911575119179647,"bss_lo":0.39944223272088597,"chart":{"base":[331.9,100.2],"fp":[195.9,329.2],"lead":"62,243.4 272,229.8 482,205 692,170.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.50 — higher than 89% of cities","fp":"low end +1pp, high end +6pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 50% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 2%; promised 78% → rained 69%"},"rel":"68.1,457 197,347.5 554.3,166.6"},"country":"IT","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.038274021352313156,"ess":296.7709142252025,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Catania</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Catania rain forecast is strongly skilful, and honest except at one point on the scale.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (95%), believe about\n<b>89%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 562 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nSIGONELLA, 17.0 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.50, ranked 15 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(5&ndash;40) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>253</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>82</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>58</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'><b>45%</b></td><td class='num'>55</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>57</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>95%</td><td class='num'><b>89%</b></td><td class='num'>57</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">1 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Catania</b> <span class=\"muted\">IT</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">honest except at one point</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.50</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>5&ndash;40\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>562 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Catania &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Catania\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/